need to build a e-commerce application ut step by step.

frontend: react
backend: nothing

implementation:
    to flush all the events like lead_generated, lead_submitted, lead_approved, lead_rejected, order_placed, order_shipped, order_delivered, scroll, href_click, banner_click, page_visit etc. we will use lambda functions to push events to the backend.
        you can use following folder "mini_server_docs" and docs about how to implement the events in the frontend and how to push them to the backend using lambda functions.
    also lambda function url and service worker version should be build like hat every time when we run github action --> generate a new build number(sw-version) it will clean all the cache and update service worker so if anything changed like frontend or lambda url endpoint etc it will get updated on frontend side.
    in document we will use indexdb--> service work flushing if events timing does not matter, if we need response or flush right now, then please create a utils fucntion like send_event_now to send the event to the backend and get the response back.

folder structure:
    work only within folder (final_code) and do not create any new folder outside it.
    storefront/ --> react based storefront, for backend we will use lambda functions to push events to the backend
    dashboard/ --> django based siple CRM

you can define a theme and color pallette for storefront as mentioned in raw_plans/design_language_guide.pdf file.


/chat page:
    copy frontend from bare-brilliant page, you can use sw events etc.. as mentioned above to push data to backend.
    on submit it will redirect to thank you page.
